2. नश् cl. 4. P. (Dhātup. xxvi, 85) न॑श्यति (rarely ˚ते and cl. 1. P. न॑शति, ˚ते; pf. ननाश, 3. pl. नेशुर्; aor. अनशत्, MBh. &c.; अनेशत्, ने॑शत्, RV.; Br. [cf. Pat. on Pāṇ. vi, 4, 120]; fut. नशिष्यति, AV.; नङ्क्ष्यति, ˚ते [cond. अनङ्क्ष्यत] MBh.; नशिता, ib.; नंष्टा, Pāṇ. vii, 2, 45; नङ्ग्धा, Vop.; inf. नशितुम्, नंष्टुम् Gr.; ind.p. नशित्वा, नष्ट्वा, नंष्ट्वा, ib.)
to be lost, perish, disappear, be gone, run away, RV. &c. &c.;
to come to nothing, be frustrated or unsuccessful, Mn.; MBh.; Kāv. &c.:
Caus. नाश॑यति, ep. also ˚ते (aor. -अनीनशत्; dat. inf. -नाशयध्यै, RV.)
to cause to be lost or disappear, drive away, expel, remove, destroy, efface, RV. &c. &c.;
to lose (also from memory), give up, MBh.; Kāv.; Pañc.;
 to violate, deflower (a girl), Daś.; Kull.;
to extinguish (a fire), BhP.;
to disappear (in मा नीनशह् and ˚नशुः), MBh. :
Desid. निनशिषति or निनङ्क्षति, Pāṇ. vii, 1, 60; 2, 45 (cf. निनङ्क्षु);
 Desid. of Caus. निनाशयिषति, to wish to destroy, Daś. :
Intens. नानश्यते or नानंष्टि Gr.

2. नस् cl. 1. Ā. (Dhātup. xvi, 26) न॑सते (aor. Pot. नसीमहि, RV. ii, 16, 8; pf. नेसे; fut. नसिता Gr.)
to approach, resort to, join, copulate (esp. as husband and wife), RV.;
to be crooked or fraudulent, Dhātup.
